+# US-01.5 – Canton for the pension fund for every employee
+
+Part of [Employee onboarding questionnaire](../feature.md), section [1. Personal details and home address](../feature.md#SEC-01-identity-and-address).
+
+**As** pension fund, **I want** the 'Canton' of every employee's registration to be known from the questionnaire answers: the canton of residence for employees living in Switzerland, and the canton of the place of work, Zurich, for employees living abroad, **so that** the required 'Canton' field is never empty, including for employees living abroad who have no canton of residence, without asking them anything for it
+
+Priority **P1** – 'Canton' is a required field; a registration with it empty is rejected. Employees living abroad (e.g. cross-border commuters) would otherwise block their registration. · Status: **decision** · Sources: F-fund_email-90df7e, F-fund_email-cb5bde, F-fund_email-a03d8c, F-pension_portal-587d3f, F-pension_portal-44a27b, F-pension_portal-b359c3, G-01, D-002
+
+> ⚠ Open questions affecting this section: [OQ-canton-abroad](../open-questions.md#oq-canton-abroad)
+Covers (details in [the section](../feature.md#SEC-01-identity-and-address) and [information.md](../information.md)): Country (home address), Canton, Canton for the pension fund
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- **AC-01.5.1 Residents of Switzerland: the canton they answered**
+  - **Given** the employee lives in Switzerland (home address country Switzerland) and has chosen their canton
+  - **When** the canton for the pension fund is determined
+  - **Then** it is the canton the employee chose, which the pension fund reads as the canton of residence. This follows D-002 provisionally; whether the canton should instead be derived from the home address is open (see OQ-canton-abroad, non-blocking).
+  - _Sources: F-fund_email-90df7e, D-002_
+
+  | Example | Country (home address) | Canton | → | Canton for the pension fund | Checked |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|
+  | Employee living in Switzerland, canton Bern (illustrative) | Switzerland | Bern | → | Bern | ✅ |
+  | Employee living in Switzerland, canton Zurich (illustrative) | Switzerland | Zurich | → | Zurich | ✅ |
+
+- **AC-01.5.2 Employees living abroad: the work canton Zurich, nothing asked**
+  - **Given** the employee's home address country is not Switzerland
+  - **When** the canton for the pension fund is determined
+  - **Then** it is Zurich, the canton of Muster AG's place of work, because employees living abroad have no canton of residence. The employee is not asked anything for it.
+  - _Sources: F-fund_email-cb5bde, F-fund_email-a03d8c, F-pension_portal-b359c3, D-002_
+
+  | Example | Country (home address) | → | Canton for the pension fund | Canton | Checked |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|
+  | Employee living in Germany (e.g. Konstanz) (illustrative) | Germany | → | Zurich | not asked | ✅ |
+  | Employee living in Liechtenstein (illustrative) | Liechtenstein | → | Zurich | not asked | ✅ |
+  | Employee living in another country (illustrative) | France | → | Zurich | not asked | ✅ |
+
